# ABD Theme Styles Pattern

Standard pattern for adding ABD theme styling to blocks and sections.

## Liquid Implementation

### 1. Assign Theme Variables

```liquid
{% liquid
  assign abd_theme = block.settings.abd_theme
  assign custom_bg = block.settings.custom_bg
  assign custom_text = block.settings.custom_text
%}
```

### 2. Apply Theme Classes to Container

```liquid
<div class="block-name {% if abd_theme != blank %}abd-theme-{{ abd_theme }}{% endif %}"
     style="{% if custom_bg != blank %}background-color: {{ custom_bg }};{% endif %} {% if custom_text != blank %}color: {{ custom_text }};{% endif %}"
     {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
  {%- if abd_theme == 'retro' -%}<div class="abd-geocities-box">{%- endif -%}
  {%- if abd_theme == 'social' -%}<div class="abd-myspace-container">{%- endif -%}
  
  <!-- Block content -->
  
  {%- if abd_theme == 'social' -%}</div>{%- endif -%}
  {%- if abd_theme == 'retro' -%}</div>{%- endif -%}
</div>
```

### 3. Use Semantic Classes

For themes to style content properly, use semantic classes:
- `.abd-title` or `h1`, `h2`, etc. - for headings
- `.abd-content` - for body text
- `.abd-header` - for header sections
- `.abd-meta` - for metadata
- `.abd-footer` - for footers
- `.abd-category` - for category tags

Example:
```liquid
{%- if block.settings.heading != blank -%}
  <div class="block-name__heading abd-title">{{ block.settings.heading }}</div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if block.settings.text != blank -%}
  <div class="block-name__text abd-content">{{ block.settings.text }}</div>
{%- endif -%}
```

